      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find $f(3)$, we need to use the given functional equation:\n\\[f(x) + 2f(1 - x) = 3x^2.\\]\n\nFirst, let's substitute $x = 3$ into the equation:\n\\[f(3) + 2f(1 - 3) = 3(3)^2.\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27. \\tag{1}\\]\n\nNext, let's substitute $x = -2$ into the equation:\n\\[f(-2) + 2f(1 - (-2)) = 3(-2)^2.\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\tag{2}\\]\n\nNow we have a system of two equations:\n1. \\(f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27\\)\n2. \\(f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12\\)\n\nTo eliminate $f(-2)$, we can multiply the first equation by 2 and then subtract the second equation from it:\n\\[2f(3) + 4f(-2) = 54,\\]\n\\[f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12.\\]\nSubtracting these two equations, we get:\n\\[2f(3) + 4f(-2) - (f(-2) + 2f(3)) = 54 - 12,\\]\n\\[3f(-2) = 42,\\]\n\\[f(-2) = 14.\\]\n\nNow substitute $f(-2) = 14$ back into the second equation:\n\\[14 + 2f(3) = 12,\\]\n\\[2f(3) = 12 - 14,\\]\n\\[2f(3) = -2,\\]\n\\[f(3) = -1.\\]\n\nThus, the value of $f(3)$ is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\).",
